 tags use. It was hardcoded here, which meant the sitemap
and the canonical tags could drift apart — and they had: the sitemap pinned
non-www while base.html mirrored whatever host the request arrived on. The old
www vs non-www split is what kept /massage/ out of Google's index.

 is emitted only for pages with a real date in sitemaps.LASTMOD. This
previously used {% now 'Y-m-d' %}, which told Google every page changed today on
every crawl -- an unreliable lastmod is discounted, so a false one actively
devalues the signal. Omitting it is better than faking it.
{% endcomment %}
{% for url in urlset %}    
        {{ canonical_origin }}{% url url.item %}
{% if url.lastmod %}        {{ url.lastmod|date:"Y-m-d" }}
{% endif %}        {{ url.changefreq }}
        {{ url.priority }}

{% endfor %}
